      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "It looks like these two images aren't really using the same settings or the same positioning, so it's hard to compare. Changes have been made since the last version, but they were done to make the camera more accurate. You can achieve a more blurred background by being further away from the background, zooming in, placing the camera further away from the subject, or going into semi auto and decreasing the aperture. The camera offers plenty of options to achieve the look you want, and most of it is based on physically accurate cameras so brushing up on real life skills can be helpful.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
