      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{60285ca04963ba22994f485b|full_name}: Hmm, so tried it out in another world and it does still pretty good I suppose. I guess my gripe was that AF just doesn't feel too good as it used to when taking a selfie shot, which I know semi-AF is for to get better adjustments I just used AF as I wanted to get nice quick shots. It's a curse being hyper-aware and bothered by minor details such as this ^^;\nFirst photo with Kimple is from 1144, second with me is 1145\nTried my best at replicating camera zoom, position, etc.\nEDIT: now that I look at the comparison shots, the second one's bokeh effect does definitely look a bit better.",
